WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.647 --> 00:00:03.250
[Interviewer] - Cindy,
Cindy, we've spoken before

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.860
but we're going to recap
everything we already talked about.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:07.920
So, where are you from originally?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.240
You grew up where?

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.640
- In Highland Park.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.473
- [Interviewer] Out here in LA?

00:00:11.473 --> 00:00:13.600
- Yeah, it's by Eagle Rock.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.540
- [Interviewer] You've
been here a long time.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.373
How many years?

00:00:15.373 --> 00:00:17.519
- [Cindy] Like 25 years or something.

00:00:17.519 --> 00:00:19.383
- [Interviewer] 25 years
and how old are you now?

00:00:19.383 --> 00:00:20.556
- [Cindy] 55.

00:00:20.556 --> 00:00:21.800
- [Interviewer] What
brought you here originally?

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.073
What were the circumstances that got you--

00:00:24.073 --> 00:00:29.073
- Using, coming down here to buy my drugs

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.110
and then go back home.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.100
- [Interviewer] And what age were you

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.950
when you first got involved in drugs?

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:37.450
- I had just turned 21.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.993
- [Interviewer] So, not a teenager.

00:00:40.446 --> 00:00:45.446
- Someone that I started
seeing introduced me to heroin

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.964
and I tried it, I didn't
even know nothing about it

00:00:49.964 --> 00:00:53.463
and that was the biggest mistake ever.

00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:55.990
- [Interviewer] Tell
me what your childhood,

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.346
you grew up with one parent, both parents?

00:00:58.346 --> 00:01:01.005
- Me and my brother, well,
we lived in Santa Monica

00:01:01.005 --> 00:01:03.300
and my mom and my dad

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.483
and my brother's younger than me,

00:01:06.749 --> 00:01:09.823
just like a regular family.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:12.630
- [Interviewer] No abuse?

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.463
No abuse?

00:01:13.463 --> 00:01:16.690
- No, no, my mom and dad,
they were good to us.

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:18.990
My dad used to take us on trips.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:23.700
We'd go to like Big Bear
or we'd go Lake Isabella.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.840
He was always taking
us places, Zuma Beach,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.880
camping and stuff to the mountains.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.870
We went to Tujunga a lot,

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.023
we used to go to Tujunga Canyon a lot.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:42.100
My dad passed away from cancer in 2010

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.070
but they were married
forever, my mom and dad.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.917
- [Interviewer] So, no
events that set you on--

00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:53.033
- No, they didn't drink,
well, my dad drank beer,

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.960
and smoked cigarettes but
nobody in my family did drugs.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:01:59.793
- [Interviewer] Is there any history

00:01:59.793 --> 00:02:00.957
of addiction in your family?

00:02:00.957 --> 00:02:01.790
- No.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.130
We weren't around it either where we lived

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.540
there wasn't like any people around

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:15.550
that I saw to like start
paying attention to it.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.453
- [Interviewer] So, for you at 21,

00:02:16.453 --> 00:02:19.180
when you first got involved in drugs,

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.250
did it just like kick in and take hold?

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.853
- [Cindy] Yeah,

00:02:22.853 --> 00:02:27.070
and I was already out of school,

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:29.730
but throughout junior
high and high school,

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.130
I still didn't know anything about heroin.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.600
I didn't know anybody
that I hung around with.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.383
I never had any boyfriends that did it.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.400
Places I went, people I saw,

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.750
or were around, in my neighborhood,

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.163
I didn't know any place that sold it.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.949
You know, it was like, it
just wasn't even thought

00:02:51.949 --> 00:02:55.422
of over there, but I knew it was bad.

00:02:55.422 --> 00:02:58.833
- [Interviewer] And what
is your drug now, heroin?

00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:01.330
Have you ever overdosed?

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:02.163
- [Cindy] No.

00:03:02.163 --> 00:03:05.099
- [Interviewer] Have
you ever gotten clean?

00:03:05.099 --> 00:03:08.395
- [Cindy] When I would get locked up.

00:03:08.395 --> 00:03:09.582
- [Interviewer] When
you ended up in prison

00:03:09.582 --> 00:03:11.670
and what did you end up in jail for?

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.675
- [Cindy] Usually it was for possession.

00:03:13.675 --> 00:03:15.964
(sirens blaring)

00:03:15.964 --> 00:03:18.420
- [Interviewer] And what
do you do for money?

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.883
- Well, there's people that help me

00:03:22.141 --> 00:03:27.141
and sometimes I'll clean tents
or something to get money

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.546
and there's a few people I date, you know?

00:03:31.546 --> 00:03:33.370
- [Interviewer] Do you have
only regular customers?

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:36.500
- Yeah, but not always.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.445
- [Interviewer] Sometimes
you'll pick up strangers.

00:03:37.445 --> 00:03:39.660
- Yeah, if I have to I have to.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.443
But, usually not.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.323
- [Interviewer] And you've
been doing this a long time.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.680
Do you have any crazy stories?

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:45.903
Things have happened.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:48.640
It's dangerous.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.500
- Yeah, it is.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:54.500
Not now, but maybe when
I was first down here

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:01.141
I got in cars a couple of times

00:04:01.141 --> 00:04:03.253
where someone pulled a gun on me.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.753
Yeah, but they started out being nice

00:04:06.753 --> 00:04:10.800
and then afterwards they put the gun away,

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.060
you know, just like to scare me with it,

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.013
but no one ever like hurt me or anything.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.070
- [Interviewer] What would you like to see

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.210
for yourself the next five years?

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:28.210
Do you imagine a different life for you?

00:04:29.192 --> 00:04:34.192
- Yeah, me and my
boyfriend that I was with,

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.410
we kind of like haven't been
together for a couple of months

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:42.340
but I kind of thought that was going

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.140
to be my last relationship

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.823
and he was going to
take me away from here.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.190
I just hope that maybe
we get back together.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:56.733
He doesn't use and we
lived together, you know,

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:00.910
get away from here

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.890
and start like a little business.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.137
- [Interviewer] So, you're sleeping where,

00:05:06.137 --> 00:05:07.210
you're not in a tent?

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:10.470
- Yeah, I got a tent, I
have a brand new tent.

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:12.280
My friend bought me a real nice one.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:14.837
- [Interviewer] You're too
well dressed to (indistinct)

00:05:14.837 --> 00:05:16.123
You gotta have something.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.263
- I'm still on the street.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.080
It's not getting any better down here.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.190
- [Interviewer] Yeah, so the heroin,

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:31.260
do you actually even
enjoy it, do you think?

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:35.600
- I've been on methadone
now for like three years

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.150
but unfortunately I'm not
all the way off of heroin.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.920
I still do it a little bit,

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.093
but the methadone does help me.

00:05:44.683 --> 00:05:47.370
But, I don't know, I
still do it a little bit.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.090
I think it's just because
I've been doing it

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:54.830
for so long that it's just
part of my way of life.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:59.830
You know, it's just part of
my routine, my daily routine.

00:06:00.176 --> 00:06:01.210
- [Interviewer] Do you have children?

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.893
- Yeah, I have two daughters
they're in Berkeley.

00:06:04.855 --> 00:06:06.770
- [Interviewer] Do you talk to them?

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:09.330
- I was talking to my big daughter

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:10.762
but she doesn't know everything.

00:06:10.762 --> 00:06:14.220
She doesn't know that I'm on the street

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:18.160
or living in a tent because
she wouldn't like it.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.623
She'd be becoming down here
trying to take me away.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.870
She's always trying to help me

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.230
and she'll send me money grams and stuff

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.720
and she'll ask me, "Mom,
can I send you things?"

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:33.870
And if she doesn't hear
from me for a little while

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.770
she gets worried and she thinks--

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:39.900
She's happy because I'm
on the methadone program,

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.275
but she doesn't know that I still use.

00:06:42.275 --> 00:06:43.440
I haven't told her,

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.793
been completely honest with her.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.120
I tell her just so much, you know,

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.560
because I'm not trying to hurt her.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.768
She worries about me a lot. (car honking)

00:06:53.768 --> 00:06:56.260
And no matter what she still loves me

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.570
she doesn't turn her back on me.

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:02.790
She just wants us to
have a good relationship

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.890
and she wants to be able
to see me all the time

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:09.090
and us to be like normal.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.099
- [Interviewer] Does
she come to visit you?

00:07:10.099 --> 00:07:12.000
- She's tried to

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.863
and I back out at the last minute.

00:07:15.993 --> 00:07:18.270
I don't know, I get scared, I guess

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:21.690
cause I don't want her to
see me in my addiction.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:25.141
You know, I just, I can't do it.

00:07:25.141 --> 00:07:26.340
I don't know.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.347
And everybody says,
Cindy, "She doesn't care.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.797
"She just wants to see her mom.

00:07:29.797 --> 00:07:30.927
"She loves you.

00:07:30.927 --> 00:07:32.847
"She doesn't care about nothing else,

00:07:32.847 --> 00:07:35.063
"where you live or, you know,

00:07:35.957 --> 00:07:37.617
"just let her see her mom.

00:07:37.617 --> 00:07:39.767
"Why are you trying to
take that from her?"

00:07:40.906 --> 00:07:43.236
But, it's just hard, you know?

00:07:43.236 --> 00:07:45.193
Cause I don't know her anymore.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.640
She's already like 27 years old.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:49.740
She's doing real good.

00:07:53.832 --> 00:07:55.860
She's a manager of a yoga studio

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:57.513
and she's massage therapist.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.930
So, she's doing really good.

00:08:02.396 --> 00:08:03.520
- [Interviewer] Well,
Cindy thank you for talking

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.084
to me again, be careful out there.

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:06.639
- [Cindy] Always a pleasure.

00:08:06.639 --> 00:08:09.097
- [Interviewer] Good luck with everything.

00:08:09.097 --> 00:08:11.043
- [Cindy] Maybe I won't be here forever

00:08:11.043 --> 00:08:13.667
but it just seems like it
cause it's been so long.

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:15.500
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

